{\xe \v packSnorm2x16\:Floating-Point Pack and Unpack Functions}
{\xe \v Floating-Point Pack and Unpack Functions\:packSnorm2x16}
\pard\plain \s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid {
{\b 
{\b GLM_FUNC_DECL} {\b uint} glm::packSnorm2x16 ({\b vec2} const & v)}}
\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAABFMH}
{\bkmkend AAAAAABFMH}
{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
First, converts each component of the normalized floating-point value v into 8- or 16-bit integer values. Then, the results are packed into the returned 32-bit unsigned integer.\par
The conversion for component c of v to fixed point is done as follows: packSnorm2x16: round(clamp(v, -1, +1) * 32767.0)\par
The first component of the vector will be written to the least significant bits of the output; the last component will be written to the most significant bits.\par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
